		{
			dependencies: [
				"4402587B0EAC4EEC"
				"45FD2226287B545E"
			]
			description: [
				"The Loot Fabrication Plant produces loot from mob predictions."
				"Unlike the Loot Fabricator you don't choose an item in the GUI but place the desired item in the input port along with the predictions. The \"blueprint\" item is not consumed."
				"For all available loot fabrications look up the uses of the Controller."
				""
				"&eController:&r a &6Simulator Modeling&r and a &6Merger Camera&r (Extra Hostile Neural Networks, see the &eHostile Neural Networks&r chapter), plus the usual 2 Redstone Servos, 2 Redstone Reception Coils, 2 Cobalt Blocks and a Manasteel Ingot."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&eLoot Fabrication Plant Tier 1 structure:&r every block is listed as a task. Check the structure preview in JEI (uses of the Controller) or let a &eMultiblock Builder&r place it for you."
				""
				"&ePorts:&r a recipe only starts if its inputs and outputs fit in the ports, so these are the sizes that run every recipe:"
				"- 1x Item Input: &eNormal&r or bigger"
				"- 1x Item Output: &eCompressed Titanic&r or bigger &7(Titanic runs 80 of 201 recipes)&r"
				""
				"Each craft returns a huge pile of loot, so the output port has to be big. Smaller output ports only run the recipes with small outputs."
				""
				"Higher tiers are optional upgrades, see the quests further out."
			]
